Schema migrations for eiye_db's metadata store.

  cd backend
  alembic current                                  # where this database is
  alembic upgrade head                             # apply pending revisions
  alembic revision --autogenerate -m "what changed"  # after editing a db.py model

The database URL comes from the application's own settings (EIYE_DATABASE_URL).
alembic.ini ships with sqlalchemy.url blank on purpose, so a deployment has
exactly one place that says which database it uses. Override a one-off with
`alembic -x url=... upgrade head`.

Editing a model without generating a revision is a bug, not a shortcut:
create_all adds missing tables and never alters an existing one, so the column
would be absent on every database that already exists.
test_migrations.py::test_migrations_match_the_models fails when the two drift.
